{% sw_extends '@QuoteManagement/storefront/page/account/quote-detail/index.html.twig' %}

{# The buyer disclosure.

   Deliberately targets `page_account_quotes_details`, NOT the more specific
   `page_account_quote_details_banner` its name suggests. That banner block
   only exists on trunk (added by SwagCommercial#2371) -- every released
   version we support, v6.7.2.0 through v6.7.12.0, has no such block, and Twig
   silently no-ops a block override the parent never declares. This is the one
   disclosure surface meant to reach the released lane too, so it has to
   extend a block that has existed since v6.7.2.0. Do not "tidy" this back to
   the narrower block; it would compile, run, and simply never render there.

   `page_account_quotes_details` wraps the whole quote body and sits inside
   SwagCommercial's own `getLicense(...) and customerHasFeature(...)` gate, so
   the banner correctly inherits that gate instead of bypassing it -- and
   `page.quote` is already in scope there. Emitted before parent() rather than
   given a block of its own, so it lands at the top of the quote body ahead of
   SwagCommercial's own content.

   The key is AgentDisclosure::MARKER_KEY, which Twig cannot import;
   StorefrontDisclosureBannerTest pins the literal on the PHP side so the two
   cannot drift apart silently.

   Deliberately not gated on quoteState: an agent that handled a quote handled
   it, and the disclosure outlives the state the quote was in at the time. #}
{% block page_account_quotes_details %}
    {% if page.quote.customFields.merchant_quote_agent_handled is defined and page.quote.customFields.merchant_quote_agent_handled %}
        {% sw_include '@Storefront/storefront/utilities/alert.html.twig' with {
            type: "info",
            heading: "merchantQuoteAgent.disclosure.banner.headline"|trans|sw_sanitize,
            content: "merchantQuoteAgent.disclosure.banner.body"|trans|sw_sanitize,
            class: " my-3"
        } %}
    {% endif %}

    {{ parent() }}
{% endblock %}
